Subject: [PATCH] Initialize visual submap ownership before opt-in LIO teardown

ONLY_LIO deliberately skips initializeVIO. The VIOManager destructor still
deletes visual_submap, so the constructor must establish null ownership.
Normal LIVO initializeVIO continues to allocate the same submap; no estimator
arithmetic, mode selection, or class layout changes.

--- a/third_party/fast_livo2/fast_livo2_core/src/vio.cpp
+++ b/third_party/fast_livo2/fast_livo2_core/src/vio.cpp
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 // FASTLIVO_DIAG_END include

 using namespace Eigen;
-VIOManager::VIOManager() {
+VIOManager::VIOManager() : visual_submap(nullptr) {
     // downSizeFilter.setLeafSize(0.2, 0.2, 0.2);
 }

# End of patch.
